# SQL migrations must always check out with LF line endings.
# sqlx checksums the whole migration file (SHA-384 over its bytes),
# so a CRLF checkout changes the checksum and the database refuses
# to open with "migration N was previously applied but has been
# modified" (seen 2026-11-28: the user's Windows clone had CRLF
# migrations while _sqlx_migrations held LF checksums for v1-v4
# and a CRLF checksum for v5).
*.sql text eol=lf
